  "answer_text": "As an AI, I don\u2019t have direct access to booking systems or payment portals to physically make a reservation for you. However, I can help you find the best way to secure or pay for a spot depending on where you are. \n\nBecause \"city center\" is highly dependent on your location, here is how you can easily reserve or pay for a spot tomorrow afternoon, with a focus on **Romania** (and options for other cities):\n\n### 1. If you are in Bucharest (or major Romanian cities):\n* **For Guaranteed Reservations (Underground Garages):** \n  You cannot pre-reserve standard street parking spots. However, if you want a guaranteed space in the strict city center (Zone 0), you can book online or via an app in major underground parking garages operated by **Interparking** (such as *Pia\u021ba Universit\u0103\u021bii*, *Intercontinental/National Theatre*, or *Cocor*). You can use the **Interparking P-app** or their website to manage this.\n* **For On-the-Spot Street Parking:** \n  If you plan to use blue-marked public street parking tomorrow afternoon, the rate in Bucharest is a flat **5 lei/hour** (or 30 lei for a full day pass). You cannot reserve these in advance, but you can pay instantly when you arrive using:\n  * **Parking Bucure\u0219ti app** (official municipal app)\n  * **TPARK** or **AmParcat** apps (highly popular and secure payment apps across Romania)\n  * **SMS** (by sending your license plate and duration to 7576 once parked).\n\n### 2. If you are in another global city:\nTo reserve a spot ahead of time tomorrow afternoon, the easiest method is to use a parking reservation platform. Depending on where you are, you can use:\n* **SpotHero** or **ParkWhiz** (Excellent for major US/Canadian city centers).\n* **Parkopedia** or **JustPark** (Great for the UK and European city centers).\n* **ParkMe** (Global coverage for finding rates and reservation links).\n\n**Want me to find the exact garage or reservation link for you?** \nJust reply with:\n1. **The city** you are in.\n2. **The specific area or landmark** in the city center you are visiting. \n3. **The approximate hours** you need the spot tomorrow afternoon.",
